# G083 — Template Maker

*v2. See `template-maker.md` for prose: the builder is itself an
editable data model, cross-reference validation between declared
slots and referenced placeholders, preview with sample data,
kind-typed validation issues, `_`-prefix reserved placeholders.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Template Editor UI

[template-editor
    IN ORDER TO
        drive an interactive UI over the TemplateBuilder data model
        surfacing cross-reference issues after every edit
        and blocking save until validation passes

    @maker <- [tm[new-maker]]

    sync @ui-events {
        create @name @category ->
            @bid <- [tm[new-template
                         {maker: @maker,
                          name: @name, category: @category}]]
            [ui[navigate-to-editor {builder-id: @bid}]]

        edit-slot @bid @slot ->
            [tm[add-slot {maker: @maker, id: @bid, slot: @slot}]]
            @issues  <- [tm[validate {maker: @maker, id: @bid}]]
            @preview <- [tm[preview  {maker: @maker, id: @bid}]]
            [ui[render-editor {issues: @issues, preview: @preview}]]

        save @bid ->
            @issues <- [tm[validate {maker: @maker, id: @bid}]]
            @issues
                where count is zero
                    @template <- [tm[freeze {maker: @maker, id: @bid}]]
                    [ecard[add-template
                            {gallery: [ecard[load-gallery]],
                             template: @template}]]
                otherwise
                    -> [ui[show-issues {issues: @issues}]]
    }
]

---

## Verb Surface

[tm
    new-maker
    new-template         {maker, name, category}       ;; -> builder-id
    add-slot             {maker, id, slot}
    remove-slot          {maker, id, slot-name}
    set-html             {maker, id, html}
    set-sample           {maker, id, slot-name, value}
    validate             {maker, id}                    ;; -> [Issue]
    preview              {maker, id}                    ;; uses sample data
    freeze               {maker, id}                    ;; -> immutable Template
                                                        ;; || has-issues
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: cross-reference validation `where` declared ≠ referenced

[tm[validate {maker: @m, id: @bid}]
    IN ORDER TO
        return a list of structured issues covering every drift between
        the declared slot list and the placeholders referenced in HTML

    @builder <- @m:builders at @bid
    @declared    <- @builder:slots mapped to name
    @referenced  <- placeholders found in @builder:html
                     excluding those beginning with "_" (reserved)

    issues <-
        @declared where not in @referenced
            -> emit #unused-slot {name: @slot-name}
      + @referenced where not in @declared
            -> emit #undeclared-placeholder {name: @placeholder}
      + @builder:slots where name is empty or contains invalid chars
            -> emit #invalid-slot-name {name}
      + @builder:slots grouped by name where count > 1
            -> emit #duplicate-slot-name {name}
      + @builder:slots where required and no sample provided
            -> emit #missing-sample {name}
]

Each issue kind is structurally distinct — the UI groups and
highlights by kind, producing specific error messages rather than
"validation failed: see logs."

## Distinctive Innate idiom: reserved names skip validation `where` prefix is "_"

[@placeholder where name begins with "_"
    -> skipped by declare-then-reference check
    -> populated at card-creation from fixed fields (_recipient, _sender)
]

Same shape as Python's `__dunder__`, Ruby's `@@class-var`, HTML's
`data-*`. A naming convention reserves a namespace without requiring
schema extensions.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @m   <- [tm[new-maker]]
    @bid <- [tm[new-template
                  {maker: @m,
                   name: "welcome", category: "greeting"}]]

    [tm[add-slot
         {maker: @m, id: @bid,
          slot: {name: "name", kind: "Text", required: true}}]]
    [tm[set-html
         {maker: @m, id: @bid,
          html: "<p>Hi {{name}}, from {{_sender}}. — {{signature}}</p>"}]]

    -> [tm[validate {maker: @m, id: @bid}]]
    ;; -> [#undeclared-placeholder {name: "signature"},
    ;;     #missing-sample {name: "name"}]

    [tm[add-slot
         {maker: @m, id: @bid,
          slot: {name: "signature", kind: "Text", required: false,
                  default: "--the Vault"}}]]
    [tm[set-sample
         {maker: @m, id: @bid, slot-name: "name",
          value: "Friend"}]]

    -> [tm[validate {maker: @m, id: @bid}]]
    ;; -> []

    -> [tm[preview  {maker: @m, id: @bid}]]
    ;; -> "<p>Hi Friend, from [preview sender]. — --the Vault</p>"
]
